<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Sarney</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1930">1930</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Sarney is a Brazilian politician and writer who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> from 1985 to 1990, the first civilian president after the military dictatorship. Elected vice-president, he took office when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tancredo-neves">Tancredo Neves</a> fell ill and died. His government oversaw the drafting of the 1988 constitution but failed to control <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">inflation</a> despite the Cruzado Plan. He later served several times as president of the Senate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-sarney.jpg" alt="José Sarney" width="320" height="467" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY 3.0 br · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jos%C3%A9_Sarney_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
